{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-logistics-route-006-01", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/Logistics/RouteOrchestratorTests.cs", "line": 378, "method": "Tick_PausedRoute_SummaryLogged_NoPerRouteTransitionLog", "category": "T3", "severity": "Low", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/Logistics/RouteOrchestrator.cs:433; let ProcessOneRoute dispatch a Paused route -> red", "what_it_asserts": "a Paused route emits no Dispatch/Wait/EndpointLost log line, keeps its status, and produces no ledger action", "why_weak": "the SummaryLogged half of the name and the leading comment (a populated store failing to emit the summary) are never asserted; the Tick: summary at RouteOrchestrator.cs:444 could stop firing entirely and the test stays green", "proposed_action": "either add an assert on the Tick: summary line (routes=1 skipped=1) or rename to Tick_PausedRoute_NoPerRouteTransitionLog and drop the summary clause from the comment", "effort": "S", "july_ref": "none"}
{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-logistics-route-006-02", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/Logistics/RouteOrchestratorTests.cs", "line": 402, "method": "Tick_MidIterationAdd_NewRoutePickedUpNextTick", "category": "T3", "severity": "Low", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/Logistics/RouteOrchestrator.cs:433; let ProcessOneRoute re-dispatch an already InTransit route -> red (the actionsAfterFirstTick + 2 assert)", "what_it_asserts": "a route added between two ticks dispatches on the second tick and the ledger grows by exactly the dispatch+debit pair", "why_weak": "the name and comment claim the per-tick snapshot isolates the iterator from an in-tick AddRoute, but routeB is added after Tick returns; deleting the snapshot copy at RouteOrchestrator.cs:404 and iterating the live list leaves this test green", "proposed_action": "rename to Tick_RouteAddedBetweenTicks_PickedUpNextTick, or drive a real mid-iteration add through the env fake's OnAnyCall hook so the snapshot copy is actually exercised", "effort": "M", "july_ref": "none"}
